For localStorage I decided to store everything as one array of note objects under a single key instead of a separate key per note,
kyunke that way I only need one getItem/setItem call and don't have to keep track of which keys exist. Each note has its own id, title, 
content, and then createdAt and updatedAt as two separate timestamps instead of one, since I wanted "last edited" to update every time
you save but still remember when the note was originally made. I wrapped the JSON.parse in a try/catch when loading, because if the
storage ever gets corrupted or someone messes with it manually, I didn't want the whole app to crash — it just falls back to an empty
list instead. Sorting by updatedAt on every render also means I didn't need a separate "pinned" or "recent" feature, editing a note naturally
bumps it to the top, which felt like the more intuitive behavior anyway.
